# Repo-root .dockerignore — excludes from EVERY docker build whose context is
# the repo root (currently: every nemo service whose Dockerfile uses
# `src/nemo/<svc>/...` relative paths). Per-image .dockerignore files exist
# under src/images/<img>/ for builds whose context is the image directory;
# those are NOT shadowed by this file, they continue to apply at their own
# scope.
#
# Goal: cut the build context from ~470M (incl. .git) to ~50M. The slowest
# image (kb-retrieval-service, Rust) ships every byte of context to the
# BuildKit daemon on every `docker buildx build .` — until this file landed,
# that included the 211M .git history that no Dockerfile ever COPYs from.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Version control / CI metadata. None of this is COPYed by any Dockerfile.
# .git alone is 211M (nearly half the repo).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.gitlab
**/.git
.hg
.svn

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editor / IDE noise. Never copied.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.history

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Language build artifacts.
# Each Dockerfile builds these fresh inside the container, so shipping the
# host's copy is pure context-transfer waste — and worse, the host artifacts
# are usually built for the wrong platform (host arch vs. container arch).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Rust
**/target
**/Cargo.lock.bak

# Node / TypeScript
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.nuxt
**/.svelte-kit
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/.eslintcache
**/.parcel-cache
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
**/pnpm-debug.log*
**/.yarn/cache
**/.yarn/install-state.gz

# Python
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*$py.class
**/*.egg-info
**/.eggs
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.tox
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov
**/.hypothesis
**/.venv
**/venv
**/env
**/ENV
**/pip-log.txt
**/pip-delete-this-directory.txt

# Go
**/vendor
**/*.test
**/*.out

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Service-local scratch / generated content that lives next to source files.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Local secrets / env overrides — never bake into images
.env.local
.env.*.local
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# Tmp / scratch
tmp
temp
**/tmp
**/temp
.cache
**/.cache

# Pre-built tarballs that shouldn't sneak into the image
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docker / Helm artifacts that never need to be inside an image.
# (Helm charts ARE part of the operator image — those are explicitly COPYed,
# so leave deployments/ alone.)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.dockerignore.bak

# Documentation rarely needs to be inside the runtime image. Most Dockerfiles
# don't COPY docs/ explicitly; but some do (e.g. operator embeds docs). Don't
# blanket-exclude — let individual Dockerfiles add their own .dockerignore.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Worktrees — Claude-driven background tasks create git worktrees alongside
# the repo. These are full copies of the tree and would double the context.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.worktrees
**/.worktrees
